{"name":"Bloodhound","hex":"#bb5511","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bloodhound","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large scenthound famed for its ability to follow a scent many days old, over vast distances. This dog is often used as a police dog to track missing people, fleeing suspects, or escaped prisoners.","A detective or other person skilled at finding people or clues."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bloodhound"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bloodhound","blocks":[{"text":"The bloodhound is a large scent hound, originally bred for hunting deer, wild boar, rabbits, and since the Middle Ages, for tracking people. Believed to be descended from hounds once kept at the Abbey of Saint-Hubert, Belgium, in French it is called le chien de Saint-Hubert."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Bloodhound_Erland22.jpg/330px-Bloodhound_Erland22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloodhound","wikidata":"Q21098"},{"title":"Bloodhound (missile)","blocks":[{"text":"The Bristol Bloodhound is a British ramjet powered surface-to-air missile developed during the 1950s. It served as the UK's main air defence weapon into the 1990s and was in large-scale service with the Royal Air Force (RAF) and the forces of four other countries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Bloodhound_SAM_at_the_RAF_Museum.jpg/330px-Bloodhound_SAM_at_the_RAF_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloodhound_(missile)","wikidata":"Q672227"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Bloodhound_2.jpg/500px-Bloodhound_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Bloodhound_2.jpg/500px-Bloodhound_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wik